<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">mobile</ansi>

The web client works on a phone. On a narrow screen it shows one view at a
time instead of side-by-side panels, and everything you can tap just types
an ordinary command for you (<ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi> describes the panels).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The bottom bar</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Game</ansi>      the story text.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Map</ansi>       the map, full screen. Drag with one finger to pan, pinch to
            zoom, and tap a room to walk there (a menu offers "Walk to
            [room]"; <ansi fg="command">help walkto</ansi>).
  <ansi fg="yellow">Here</ansi>      the room you stand in (exits, who is here, gathering progress),
            the game clock, and the tutorial while you take the course.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Company</ansi>   the dock: health, and the Character, Company, Combat and Comm
            tabs, scrolled sideways if they do not all fit.
  The cog opens the client's settings.

  The command box and the touch bar stay on screen in every view, so you
  can walk and type while you watch the map.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The touch bar</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">N S E W U D</ansi>   go that way (<ansi fg="command">north</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">south</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">east</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">west</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">up</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">down</ansi>).
  <ansi fg="yellow">Walk to...</ansi>    lists the named places on the map, nearest first (the same
                 places <ansi fg="command">walkto</ansi> understands); pick one and your company
                 walks there. While a walk is under way the list starts with
                 "Stop walking" and a <ansi fg="yellow">Stop</ansi> button appears (<ansi fg="command">walkto stop</ansi>).
  <ansi fg="yellow">Look, Inventory, Status, Camp</ansi>   type those commands.
  The small arrow at the left folds the bar away and brings it back.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Battles</ansi>

  The battle screen fills the phone. Retreat and the company focus buttons
  (the only things you can change mid-battle) are one tap each. Your
  allies' companies show as small pennants at the top of the picture: tap
  one to watch that company full size, and tap your own band to come back
  (<ansi fg="command">help battlescreen</ansi>). Minimise shrinks the picture to a badge above the
  bottom bar.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Installing it</ansi>

  The client can be installed like an app. In Chrome on Android, open the
  menu and choose "Install app" (or "Add to Home screen"); in Safari on an
  iPhone or iPad, tap Share, then "Add to Home Screen". It then opens
  without the browser's address bar, under the Ashveil icon. It still needs
  a connection to the game; it does not play offline.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help walkto</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help worldmap</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help battlescreen</ansi>.
